<title>USA: Maine Public Service Co Q1 shr loss $0.16.</title>
<headline>Maine Public Service Co Q1 shr loss $0.16.</headline>
<dateline>PRESQUE ISLE, Me. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.16   profit	 $0.90</p>
<p> Net loss		     254   profit	 1,451</p>
<p> Oper revs		 15,368		   15,756</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   1,617		    1,617</p>
<p>	 12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.25     loss	 $2.93</p>
<p> Net profit	     406,157     loss	 4,738</p>
<p> Oper revs		 57,007		   55,315</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	 1,617		    1,617</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Quarters ended March 31.</p>
<p>Earnings for for Q1, 1997 reflect the cost of additional replacement power associated with the unscheduled Maine Yankee outage, which reduced earnings by $0.77 per share. Additional capacity expense to address issues identified in an Independent Safety Assessment further reduced earnings by $0.26 per share.</p>
<p>The outage at Yankee Maine is expected to continue, said the company, until summer.</p>
<p>Extraordinary charges in the 12 months ended March 1996, totaled $2.00 per share.</p>
